          so every jar shipped at compile/runtime scope is under a license MOSIP allows
          (see the matrix in licenses/NOTICE). "MOSIP: Yes" below means allowed by that matrix.
          nfiq2.0 has the same runtime dependencies as nfiq1.0 minus Lombok, plus a direct
          org.openpnp:opencv dependency and jackson-module-afterburner
          (needed by kernel-core ExceptionUtils, which Nfiq2Exception uses).
          The one exception to the matrix is the FingerJetFX OSE port inside nfiq2.0 (LGPL-3.0).
          JJ2000 (jai-imageio-jpeg2000) is not in the matrix and is marked "to be reviewed".
          CI (.github/workflows/push-trigger.yml) builds and publishes the parent POM and both
          libraries together from the repository root.

